<p>The initial premise seems intriguing, but I'm not fully sold on how it is presented. It feels like you're using this to present two different ideas with barely connected threads in one article; a documentary series that's somewhat anomalous in nature, and GRU-P happenings. In fact, I almost didn't really understand how the final addendum connected with the rest of the article, and even now, it just feels like it's there only to be there. Despite the fact that it's interesting, I can't say I'm really sold on the article as a whole.</p>
<p>Here are my tastes in entertainment speaking: I think stopping where you did with presenting Frozen Steel isn't enough. I'd love to know more about this show, where the Foundation could realistically and reasonably know more. I think there's a lot going on you barely touch on or imply that would be entertaining in its own right. Though you risk dragging the article on more, it'd be more of an engaging read as a result. Maybe it could even help establish a stronger connection with what GRU-P is up to and make the second addendum seem less&#8230; there.</p>

