														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2433437">
									

<p>So there is a lot to like in this article for me. The contents of the show remind me of a much more anomalous version of the reality shows that have taken over the History and Discovery channel here in the US, but unlike those shows this one has a concept that is both more terrifying and more entertaining. The statistics that you provided (massive wr ships slamming into the cost line at 900km/h, at least 100 ships arriving every day, etc) made me do a double take as the area in the documentary becomes less of a ship yard and more of a shooting gallery with the world’s largest railgun. Additionally, I though the name of the MTF was pretty clever.</p>
<p>If I did have one nitpick, it would be that the last addenda begins to lose me a bit. What I gathered from that, was that the ships in this documentary are those ships being “smashed upon the sea” by the Tsar’s wild dancing, but I’m not sure. It’s not enough for me to dislike this article, but it left me scratching my head.</p>
<p>Overall +1.</p>
<p>One final question though. Why Ron Perlmen. I’m just curious.</p>

